/**
 * Plan 00B-3 C0 — the executable derivability contract.
 *
 * An 00C-style builder consuming ONLY the five-key allowlisted completion
 * snapshot must reconstruct the complete family evidence the 00C fold
 * consumes. The contract is pinned three ways:
 *   1. SCHEMA drift — the code registry/enums byte-agree with the
 *      pre-authored schema artifact (authored BEFORE implementation).
 *   2. TWO-SIDED FIXTURE — hand-authored snapshot fixtures deep-equal their
 *      hand-computed expected projections (never generated by the projector
 *      under test).
 *   3. LIVE COMPOSITION — sessions composed through the REAL lifecycle
 *      hooks/ledgers satisfy the three-way agreement invariant: the
 *      latched-snapshot reconstruction and the frozen-ledger projection
 *      agree (comparable subset), across accepted AND rejected ask
 *      transitions, deliveries, playbacks, invalid state and round usage.
 *
 * The four open cycle-5 findings of the 00B-2 hold are MANDATORY NAMED
 * CASES here (proven RED against the branch tip before their fixes landed —
 * recorded in the execution log):
 *   F1 — rejected ask transitions must not publish as valid lifecycle
 *        evidence (acceptance-gated sub-records, C1);
 *   F2 — open Tier-2 asks must hold the completion freeze (C2);
 *   F3 — delivery/playback rows must carry the SEMANTIC family with
 *        transport as a separate field (C3);
 *   F4 — lives in plan00-frame-parity-matrix.test.js (observation
 *        update/recode scenario legs).
 * C5's projection fields (api_transport, delivery refs/aliases, ACK-body
 * hashes, freeze-time invalid rows, the unconsumed-provisional fold) are
 * asserted here as further contract cases.
 */

